BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:processing-foundation-fellowship-2027@papers.aesthetic.computer
DTSTAMP:20261019T000000Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261029T000000Z
DTSTART:20261102T075900Z
SUMMARY:Processing Foundation Fellowship 2027 — deadline
DESCRIPTION:An eight-month fellowship for artists\, educators and engineers
  building open-source tools and resources for the arts\, in three tracks: 
 Gaming the System (an open-source game-design toolkit co-designed with und
 erserved young people in Los Angeles\, backed by the Riot Games Social Imp
 act Fund)\, Collective Intelligence (youth AI education with the Mark Cuba
 n Foundation) and DIY Computing (cyberdecks in New York). Every project mu
 st build on p5.js\, the p5.js Editor or Processing.\n\nPlus open-source me
 ntorship\, a cohort\, professional development and public programs.\nFee n
 ot stated\n\nEligibility: US-based nominees only\; self-nomination is welc
 ome. Gaming the System is hybrid in Los Angeles\, for game makers\, creati
 ve coders and educators based there\; DIY Computing is hybrid in New York\
 ; Collective Intelligence is remote anywhere in the US.\n\nDeadline: 2026-
 11-01. Nominations close 11:59 PM PST\; invited nominees submit proposals 
 by November 23\n\nVideo interviews the week of December 7\; fellows notifi
 ed the week of December 14\; final presentations October 2\, 2027.\n\nOffi
 cial call: https://processingfoundation.org/programs/fellowships/fellowshi
 p-2027/\nChecked 2026-10-29
URL:https://processingfoundation.org/programs/fellowships/fellowship-2027/
LOCATION:United States (hybrid in New York or Los Angeles\, or remote)
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
